# Cloudflare response headers.
#
# Format: a path pattern on its own line, then indented "Header: value" lines.
# Comments must start at column 0 - an indented "#" is read as a header line.
#
# Note on the missing _redirects file: Workers static assets validates that
# file and rejects any rule with a hostname in it ("Only relative URLs are
# allowed"), unlike Pages which accepts them. The www-to-apex redirect
# therefore lives in the dashboard: Rules -> Redirect Rules. See the README.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()

# No Content-Security-Policy on purpose. AdSense and GA4 load scripts and
# frames from a shifting set of Google domains, and a policy written before ads
# are live is the kind that quietly stops them serving weeks later. Add one
# once ads are running, and test it with ads enabled.

# Hashed filenames, so these can be cached indefinitely.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# These change without changing name, so they must revalidate.
/sitemap.xml
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/robots.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

/ads.txt
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
